<DocsLayout title="Maintaining" description="Telemetry, coverage audits, PR gates, and session-end protocol in engrams.">
  <h1>Maintaining: Telemetry, Coverage &amp; Curation</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Maintenance in Engrams is continuous and measurable. Instead of passive knowledge decay,
    Engrams uses <strong>retrieval telemetry</strong> to identify vocabulary gaps, <strong>coverage audits</strong>
    to prevent unanchored code, and <strong>enforced PR gates</strong> at session close.
  </p>

  <h2 class="reveal">1. Usage Telemetry &amp; Curation — <code>engrams usage</code></h2>
  <p>
    Engrams automatically logs every retrieval command (<code>query</code>, <code>relevant</code>, <code>advise</code>, <code>brief</code>).
    The <code>usage</code> command exposes call counts and trends:
  </p>
  <pre><code>engrams usage
engrams usage --since 2w --daily</code></pre>

  <p>Example response:</p>
  <pre><code>&#123;
  "total_calls": 73,
  "commands": &#123;
    "advise": &#123; "calls": 34, "constraints_fired": 89, "distinct_targets": 3 &#125;,
    "relevant": &#123; "calls": 21, "decisions_surfaced": 67 &#125;,
    "query": &#123; "calls": 18, "zero_hit": 4 &#125;,
    "brief": &#123; "calls": 5, "hits": 5 &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;</code></pre>

  <h3 class="reveal">The Zero-Hit Curation Loop</h3>
  <p>
    Zero-hit queries are the single most valuable telemetry signal — each miss represents a vocabulary
    gap that likely caused an agent to fall back to an expensive file dump. <code>engrams usage --misses</code>
    ranks these gaps so maintainers can add missing tags or anchors:
  </p>
  <pre><code>engrams usage --misses</code></pre>
  <pre><code>&#123;
  "hint": "each miss is a search that found nothing — a vocabulary gap that likely triggered a file-dump fallback",
  "misses": [
    &#123; "query": "outlook", "count": 2 &#125;,
    &#123; "query": "system_user_id", "count": 1 &#125;
  ]
&#125;</code></pre>

  <h2 class="reveal">2. Knowledge Health &amp; Access Stats — <code>decision stats</code></h2>
  <p>
    Verify which architectural decisions are actively earning their keep vs. candidates for consolidation:
  </p>
  <pre><code>engrams decision stats --most-accessed --limit 5
engrams decision stats --never-accessed</code></pre>

  <h2 class="reveal">3. Knowledge Coverage Audits — <code>engrams coverage</code></h2>
  <p>
    Before shipping feature work or refactors, verify what fraction of files have live anchored decisions and how close the nearest guidance is:
  </p>
  <pre><code># Check a directory
engrams coverage src/

# Audit changed files on a PR branch
engrams coverage --diff main...HEAD</code></pre>

  <p>Example response:</p>
  <pre><code>&#123;
  "files": 14,
  "anchored": 10,
  "anchored_pct": 0.714,
  "dead_anchors": [],
  "median_hops": 1.0
&#125;</code></pre>

  <h2 class="reveal">4. Session Closure &amp; PR Gates — <code>engrams session close</code></h2>
  <p>
    At the end of a session, record the reads your knowledge graph prevented and validate that PRs are properly connected to decisions and source files:
  </p>
  <pre><code>engrams session close \
  --reads-skipped 14 \
  --reads-required 2 \
  --tokens-saved 70000 \
  --pr 42 \
  --note "Designed Stripe adapter using Provider contract"</code></pre>

  <div class="callout tip reveal">
    <strong>Enforced PR Gate:</strong> When <code>--pr</code> is supplied, <code>session close</code> <strong>refuses to close</strong>
    unless the PR node is linked to at least one architectural decision and connected to anchored source files.
  </div>

  <p>To inspect cumulative token ROI and past sessions:</p>
  <pre><code>engrams session history</code></pre>

  <h2 class="reveal">5. PR Reverse Lookup — <code>engrams pr find</code></h2>
  <p>
    Find which decisions, patterns, or progress entries reference a specific PR number or URL:
  </p>
  <pre><code>engrams pr find 42</code></pre>

  <h2 class="reveal">6. Structural Health — <code>engrams doctor</code></h2>
  <p>
    Run project-wide integrity checks across all records:
  </p>
  <pre><code>engrams doctor</code></pre>
  <ul>
    <li>Dead file anchors (anchors pointing to deleted or moved files).</li>
    <li>Dangling manual links.</li>
    <li>Decisions with Git staleness drift.</li>
    <li>Unconfirmed consolidation patterns (&gt;180 days old).</li>
    <li>Cycles in transitive relationships (<code>causes</code>, <code>supersedes</code>, <code>depends_on</code>).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="reveal">Session End Protocol (PR Close-Back)</h2>
  <ol class="loop reveal">
    <li class="loop-step">
      <span class="loop-num">1</span>
      <h3>Enumerate</h3>
      <p><code>git diff --name-only &lt;base&gt;...HEAD</code> to list changed paths.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="loop-step">
      <span class="loop-num">2</span>
      <h3>Decide</h3>
      <p>Log decisions for all durable design choices with <code>--contract</code>.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="loop-step">
      <span class="loop-num">3</span>
      <h3>Anchor &amp; Link</h3>
      <p>Attach file anchors (<code>anchor add</code>) and PR references (<code>pr add</code>).</p>
    </li>
    <li class="loop-step">
      <span class="loop-num">4</span>
      <h3>Rebuild</h3>
      <p><code>engrams graph rebuild</code> turns anchors into code-node edges.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="loop-step">
      <span class="loop-num">5</span>
      <h3>Close &amp; Export</h3>
      <p><code>engrams session close --pr &lt;n&gt;</code> validates the PR gate and <code>engrams export</code> commits markdown.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</DocsLayout>

